      "extract": "Given a set A write SA for the symmetric group on A, i.e., the group of bijections of A. For σ ∈SA and a ∈A we always write aσ for the image of a under σ. In other words, we choose to write maps in SA on the right of their argument. This means that στ (for σ, τ ∈SA) is deﬁned by a(στ) = (aσ)τ. We will write Sr as a shorthand for S{1,...,r}. Consider the group Γ = GL(V ) of linear automorphisms on an n- dimensional",
